build.claude/
*.exe

# mercurius design-review rounds. Generated per review, and the decisions that
# came out of them live in docs/ instead.
.mercurius/

# Files pasted or dropped into a session from the board. Landed here rather
# than in the working directory root so that one line covers them forever and a
# screenshot never turns up in `git status`.
.atrium/

# the daemon's own state
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm

# scratch notes, not part of the project
bug.md
*.exe~
*.test
*.out
coverage.txt

# editor / IDE
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# ANCHORED, or it matches every directory of that name at any depth. Unanchored
# it also swallowed `scripts/walkthrough`, which holds recorded walkthroughs
# that ARE meant to be checked in, and a file nobody can see in `git status` is
# a file nobody knows is not committed.
/walkthrough
docs/backlog

# Notes comparing atrium to another tool. Local only, on purpose: they name a
# third party, quote its documentation, and say where it is ahead of us. That is
# a reasonable thing to write for yourself and not a thing to publish from this
# repository. What comes OUT of one is a backlog item that stands on its own and
# names nobody.
*-comparison*.md
# Playwright, which is not a dependency of atrium and is installed only when
# somebody wants to watch a recorded walkthrough. The specs under
# scripts/walkthrough ARE checked in. What it downloads and what it produces
# are not: a browser is 200MB and a video is an artefact of one run.
node_modules
package-lock.json
test-results
